.TH FILESTREAM 3 "2026" "y-- standard library" "y-- Library Reference"
.SH NAME
FileStream \- file I/O module
.SH DESCRIPTION
Opens files for reading and writing.
A file handle returned by \fBOpen\fR or \fBSafeOpen\fR exposes the methods
\fBRead\fR, \fBReadLines\fR, \fBWrite\fR, \fBClear\fR, \fBClose\fR, and \fBIsOpen\fR
(documented in the \fBfile\fR value-type reference).
.SH FUNCTIONS
.SS Open
.TP
\fBSYNOPSIS\fR
.br
file() Open(path: string())
.TP
\fBDESCRIPTION\fR
Opens the file at
.I path
for reading and writing.
Returns a file handle.
Raises \fBFileNotFoundError\fR if the file cannot be opened.
.TP
\fBARGUMENTS\fR
.TP
path (string())
Filesystem path to open.
.TP
\fBRETURN VALUE\fR
file() \- an open file handle.
.TP
\fBERRORS\fR
.br
\fBArgumentError\fR \- wrong number of arguments (must be 1).
.br
\fBFileNotFoundError\fR \- file not found or permission denied.
.TP
\fBEXAMPLES\fR
.EX
Open("data.txt")       -> <file handle>
.EE
.SS SafeOpen
.TP
\fBSYNOPSIS\fR
.br
file() SafeOpen(path: string(), fallback: any() = none())
.TP
\fBDESCRIPTION\fR
Tries to open the file at
.I path .
Returns
.I fallback
(default: none()) instead of throwing if the file cannot be opened.
.TP
\fBARGUMENTS\fR
.TP
path (string())
Filesystem path to open.
.TP
fallback (any())
Returned on failure; defaults to none().
.TP
\fBRETURN VALUE\fR
file() on success, or
.I fallback
on failure.
.TP
\fBERRORS\fR
\fBArgumentError\fR \- if called with 0 or more than 2 arguments.
.TP
\fBEXAMPLES\fR
.EX
SafeOpen("maybe.txt")            -> <file handle> or none()
SafeOpen("missing.txt", false)   -> false
.EE
.SH "SEE ALSO"
file(3), Os(3)
